    {
      "key": "how_to_play",
      "text": "How to play",
      "tags": ["immutable"],
      "play": { "phases": [] },
      "tooltip": "Click one of your pieces to light up the squares it can reach, then click a square to move. Click an enemy piece to take it — its square lights up too.\n\nCastling: the two buttons beside your graveyard. Needs king and rook both unmoved, and the squares between them empty.\n\nNot implemented yet:\n- Check and checkmate. You win by capturing the king, and nothing stops you moving into check or castling through it.\n- En passant.\n- Pawn promotion. A pawn reaching the far rank just stops there.\n- Draws: stalemate, threefold repetition, the fifty-move rule.\n- Resigning and offering a draw."
    },
